\custom slash=My _element=mark _classes=.b-y
\custom slash=Mg _element=mark _classes=.b-lg
\custom slash=Mp _element=mark _classes=.b-p

<style>
.b-y {background-color:yellow;}
.b-lg {background-color:lightgreen;}
.b-p{background-color:pink;}
</style>

!! Self-nesting works (regression of v0.x test-inline-nesting-mark)

We initially marked same-marker self-nesting as out-of-scope. Empirically it works after the symbol-greediness fix in `registry.js` excluded the close marker's first char from the symbol regex.

!!! Bare nest (no symbols)

a /° outer /° inner °/ outer °/ z

!!! Three-deep, three different symbols on the same marker

The pragmas at the top register `My`, `Mg`, `Mp` as `<mark>` elements with different background classes. Same source as the v0.x [[test-inline-nesting-mark]]:

Highlight using mark in /°My yellow°/ or /°Mg light green°/ or /°Mp pink°/.

Nested: Highlight in /°My yellow°/ or /°Mg light /°My yel/°Mp pink°/low°/ green°/ or /°Mp pink°/.

!!! Cross-marker for comparison

Three different markers nested: ❮ A /° B ⠒ C ⠶ B °/ A ❯ end.